        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          A positive slope indicates an upward incline where elevation increases from left to right. A negative slope marks a downward descent where elevation drops over forward distance. A horizontal plane has a rise of zero, producing a slope of zero. A vertical wall has a horizontal run of zero, producing an undefined mathematical slope because dividing any real number by zero is impossible.
