          A persistent misconception among homeowners and novice builders is assuming that a 100% slope represents a vertical cliff or 90-degree wall. In mathematics and civil surveying, a 100% slope simply indicates that vertical rise exactly equals horizontal run. When a path ascends one meter over one meter of horizontal distance, the ratio equals one. The inverse tangent of one is 45 degrees.
        </p>

